    "lawCode": "Amd §2808, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2238\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to requiring specific\nreserved bed days for veterans, spouses of veterans, widows of veterans,\nGold Star Parents and their dependents who are cared for at the New York\nState Veterans' Homes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to establish a reserved bed day policy for\npersons residing in State Veterans' Homes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision 25 of section 2808 of public health, by\nestablishing a reserved bed day policy for veterans, spouses of veter-\nans, widows of veterans, Gold Star Parents and their dependents who are\ncared for at the New York State Veterans' Homes.\n\nSection 2 is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nSome veterans in State Veterans' Homes may require additional temporary\ncare or hospitalization at another facility. This legislation provides\nsome leeway to allow them to keep their spot in the Veterans' Home if\nthey return within 10 days. It applies to spouses of veterans, widows of\nveterans, Gold Star Parents and their dependents. In order to qualify\nfor medical coverage for reserved bed days, the person must have resided\nfor at least thirty days since the date of his or her initial admission;\nthe part of the facility must have a vacancy rate of no more than five\npercent on the first day the person is hospitalized or on therapeutic\nleave of absence.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law. Effective immediately the addition, amendment, and/or\nimplementation of his act on or before its effective date are authorized\nto be made and completed on or before such effective date.\n",
