    "lawCode": "Amd §2808, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2238B\n\nSPONSOR: BROOKS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to requiring specific\nreserved bed days at the New York State Veterans' Homes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to establish a reserved bed day policy for\npersons residing in State Veterans' Homes.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends subdivision 25 of section 2808 of public health, by\nestablishing a reserved bed day policy for veterans, spouses of veter-\nans, widows of veterans, Gold Star Parents and their dependents who are\ncared for at the New York State Veterans' Homes.\n\nSection 2 is the enacting clause.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nFrom time to time, some veterans residing in State Veterans' Homes may\nrequire additional temporary care or hospitalization at another facili-\nty. In the event they must seek temporary care elsewhere this legis-\nlation provides some leeway to save their spot in the Veterans' Home by\nreserving their bed. In order to qualify for medical coverage for\nreserved bed days, the person must have resided for at least thirty days\nsince the date of his or her initial admission.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\n$400,000 - $500,000 to the State's Medicaid System annually\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law. Effective immediately the addition, amendment, and/or\nimplementation of his act on or before its effective date are authorized\nto be made and completed on or before such effective date.\n",
